            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LORRIE56"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Read \"The Subtle Art of Perfect Pancakes\" on this site. This article has several tips, one of which is to refrigerate the batter for a while to allow the gluten to settle down and let the baking powder start to act, resulting in fluffy pancakes. Also , do not stir before using as this pops all the little bubbles created from the sitting. Interesting, huh!?! Anyway, except for a little vanilla, made recipe as it reads and I was happy with them."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "diz10us"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my go to pancake recipe. Have been making these for years. I add a tablespoon of white vinegar to the milk to make it buttermilk pancakes and refrigerate the mix overnight. Perfect every time.",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-21T21:21:56.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessica Lynn Lambson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "First I whipped the eggs then added the milk and the oil. then I added the sugar. Then I added the rest of the dry ingredients. Afterward, I added two teaspoons of vanilla extract (made 9 servings) to add a touch of sweet. It turned out really yummy. Thanks!~",
            "datePublished": "2018-10-04T01:28:33.857Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jenn D Hetherington"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Into my recipe book they go. Perfect pancakes. Made the original recipe for my boyfriend, then made myself a gluten free batch using 1 1/3 cup freshly ground oat flour (I grind my own), and they both turned out wonderful. I use a nonstick pan not greased, as I found the batter to spread too far when using oil. And I start on medium heat and end up turning it down a bit. But it all depends on your pan and stovetop! They can also be frozen, then I thaw them a bit and toss them in the toaster for a quick breakfast or snack. I made a second batch just to freeze, and gave a celiac friend the recipe for my gf rendition the same day I first made them.",
            "datePublished": "2019-11-09T05:51:49.820Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tcasa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A great basic recipe. The batter was thin. I would recommend sifting the flour and letting the batter rest for at least 5 minutes or so. With that said my kids devoured these pancakes. Update: I made these again and reduced the milk to 3/4 cup without sifting. Much better!",
            "datePublished": "2017-10-23T14:58:35.960Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bkat99"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Marvelous. Let sit 15-30 mins to make bubbles and don't re-stir before pouring. Added chocolate chips while cooking and it came out wonderful.",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-21T22:14:21.017Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ronna"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good. It is nice to find a recipe that makes a nice amount for just 2 people. This made 6 medium pancakes which the 2 of us had with bacon. Lovely Sunday breakfast. I put the wet ingredients in the blender, quick whiz, then the dry, whiz again, then let rest for 15-20 minutes. Easy to pour.",
            "datePublished": "2018-01-14T11:40:06.533Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
